      {
        "introduction": "What a disheartening experience this must be for Jeremiah—off in a foreign country, separated from his scattered family, and surrounded by idolatrous Hebrews who have not even begun to learn the lesson of Judah’s fall. Now in his older years Jeremiah must indeed have a broken heart. But surely in the kingdom of the Messiah about whom he has confidently prophesied he will receive great reward."
